/**
 * Per-control catalog-sourceFile override (Phase 9 D-20 mechanism).
 *
 * Some workbook col-E `sourceLinks[]` entries point at the wrong config file.
 * Rather than mutate `LZA_UC_BASENAME_MAP` (Option (a), REJECTED — would
 * break every other control keyed on the same basename) or extend the
 * bbfa30a `repoRelativePathBasename` ENOENT-fallback (Option (c), REJECTED —
 * couples extractor semantics to the loader), we redirect specific controlIds
 * at `seed.ts:loadFile` BEFORE `repoRelativePath` runs. The redirected value
 * is the FULL repo-relative path (not a basename), so it bypasses catalog
 * `sourceLinks[]` resolution entirely for the listed controlIds.
 *
 * Consumers:
 * - `seed.ts:loadFile` — consults `PER_CONTROL_SOURCE_FILE_OVERRIDE[record.controlId]`
 *   BEFORE `repoRelativePath`. On match, `relPath` = the override value and
 *   the emitted `Fingerprint.sourceFile` field uses `basename(overrideRel)`
 *   (D-19 truthfulness — downstream `validate-health` inferredReasons buckets
 *   by sourceFile).
 *
 * Discipline:
 * - Key is the EXACT `record.controlId` (e.g. `LZA-G-CT-1`, not `G-CT-1` or
 *   `LZA-G-CT-01`). Typos silently fall through to the catalog hint —
 *   RESEARCH § 8 Pitfall 1. `seed.test.ts` D-20/D locks the exact-string
 *   contract.
 * - Value is a repo-relative POSIX path under the UC checkout root; it is
 *   resolved via `safeResolveUnderBase` downstream so `..` / absolute paths
 *   are rejected.
 * - This map is opt-in per-controlId. Every non-listed controlId flows
 *   through the unmodified `repoRelativePath` → bbfa30a-fallback path.
 *
 * Seeded entries (Phase 9 Wave 1):
 * - LZA-G-CT-1/2/3 → `modules/base/default/global-config.yaml`
 *   Catalog col-E says `organization-config.yaml`, but the `controlTower:`
 *   block lives in `global-config.yaml`. Verified against
 *   `/tmp/lza-uc-1.3.1/modules/base/default/global-config.yaml:69-226` per
 *   Phase 9 RESEARCH § 2 A1/A2/A3 (HIGH confidence).
 *
 * Post-Phase-12 remediation (quick 260914-fr8):
 * - LZA-SEC-SSM-4/6 → `modules/base/default/security-config.yaml`
 *   Catalog col-E hints `global-config.yaml`, but `ssmSettings` +
 *   `ssmAutomation` live under `centralSecurityServices` in
 *   `security-config.yaml:677-685`. Same D-20 semantics.
 * - LZA-SEC-DPPE-4/5 → `modules/base/default/organization-config.yaml`
 *   Catalog col-E hints `security-config.yaml`, but `taggingPolicies`
 *   (organization-config.yaml:124) and `backupPolicies` (line 149) are
 *   top-level keys in `organization-config.yaml`. Reclassifies DPPE-4/5
 *   from "legit-inferred / cross-file-deferred" to "matchable" via the
 *   same D-20 mechanism used for G-CT-1/2/3 and SSM-4/6.
 * See `.planning/debug/inferred-extractor-classification.md` real-bug
 * bucket taxonomy `sourceFile-mismatch`.
 */
